            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "FBA"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This was a nice change from having a lettuce salad. It was nice and crunchy. I served the sliced red onion on the side to be added to the dish as my husband doesn't like raw onions. I think next time I make this, I'll add cherry or grape tomatoes for color and taste. I'd also suggest chopping the broccoli florets into slightly smaller pieces."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Sarah Jo"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I only used half of one small red onion--I didn't want the salad to be overpowered by onion. I also made this into a creamy salad by adding a quarter cup of reduced fat sour cream to the italian dressing before tossing it with the salad ingredients. Nice basic salad. I'd make this again. I think this would be good with bacon and a little shredded cheddar cheese, too.",
            "datePublished": "2012-07-08T06:38:13.830Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "steph"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I chopped the broccoli and cauliflower to similar sizes, left out the onion since my mother hates them and added feta cheese crumbles. Fabulous! I’ve made it with and without the sunflower seeds - both are great!",
            "datePublished": "2024-07-09T17:23:42.076Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "rgirl"
            },
            "reviewBody": "With so much Cauliflower and Broccoli being around from the farmers markets this time of year, I'm always looking for new ideas for these. This salad was just wonderful! I used chopped walnuts and raisins (as another reviewer suggested) along with grape tomatoes and those along with a good quality natural Italian dressing really brought the flavors together into a great balance. This turned out to be a truly tasty side salad that was enjoyed by all. It is also very high in nutrients. I will make this one again and again. Thanks to the original author for making this fine recipe available.",
            "datePublished": "2009-11-02T17:27:01.087Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "larkspur"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is an extremely easy salad to put together. The flavor is a but too light, but pleasant at the same time. I didn't have any red onion, so I used green instead. I also added some celery, but other than that, I made no changes to the recipe. My family ate this salad, but no one raved about it. However, it is very healthy and I might make it again. Oh...I used a homemade (kind of...it was the Good Seasonings packet!) Italian dressing...if I make this again, I might use more than half a cup to give the salad more flavor. Thanks for sharing the recipe!",
            "datePublished": "2010-06-13T05:44:01.263Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "JANDC1927"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I did this as a stir fry and it was wonderful!",
            "datePublished": "2006-03-12T13:29:27.933Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
